ibmveth_pool_resize.py
======================

Description
-----------
Validates that the IBM Virtual Ethernet (ibmveth) driver correctly handles
resizing each receive-buffer pool (pool0 through pool4) to 65536 bytes while
background flood-ping traffic is running, with no kernel call traces or OOM
events.

The ibmveth driver exposes five receive-buffer pools via sysfs:

  /sys/class/net/<iface>/device/pool<N>/size    - buffer size in bytes (r/w)

This test writes a target value (default 65536) to each pool's size knob one
at a time, scans dmesg for call traces or OOM events, then restores the
original value before moving on to the next pool.


Parameters
----------
See ibmveth_pool_resize.yaml for full parameter documentation.

Key parameters:

  interface       ibmveth interface name or MAC address  (REQUIRED)
  host_ip         IP address to assign to the interface   (REQUIRED)
  netmask         Netmask for host_ip                     (REQUIRED)
  peer_ip         Peer machine IP address                 (REQUIRED)
  peer_user       SSH username on the peer                (default: root)
  peer_password   SSH password on the peer                (REQUIRED)
  ping_count      Total packets for background flood-ping (default: 1000000)
  pool_size       Buffer size in bytes written to each
                  pool's size knob                        (default: 65536)

